# Prysm

**One idea in. Every model's language out.**

Prysm is a rule-based image-prompt optimizer. You describe a rough idea, pick what you're making, tune a few knobs, and Prysm refracts it into the native prompt grammar of five different image models — front-loaded weighted phrases with parameters for **Midjourney**, full natural-language scene prose for **Nano Banana / GPT-Image**, text-first phrasing for **Ideogram**, dense descriptive clauses for **Flux**, and an explicit style family for **Recraft**.

No build step, no dependencies, no API keys, no backend. It's a single HTML file that runs entirely in the browser. Nothing you type leaves the page.

## What it does

- **Five categories**, each with its own tailored scaffolding: poster, brand image, UGC, logo, and brand promo. UGC fakes authentic imperfection; logo strips out photographic detail and forces a spelled-correct text directive; poster and promo expose headline fields — the structure changes to match what you're making.
- **A style layer** that composes on top — mood, palette, lighting, medium/render, aspect ratio, and detail intensity (which actually drives the Midjourney stylize value and descriptor density, not just a label).
- **One semantic representation, five serializers.** Every input feeds a single internal model of your idea, then each target model's serializer renders it into that model's dialect — so the outputs stay coherent with each other.
- **Top-grade starts** — five hand-tuned concept presets per category. Tap one to load it, or hit Surprise for a random pull. Randomization is *guarded*: each category has its own legal pool, so a roll never hands a logo studio lighting or gives UGC a rich studio render.
- **Locks.** Pin any field — your idea or any knob — and rolls leave it untouched. Pin the idea and Surprise just reshuffles the styling around your fixed concept.
- **History rail.** Your last six rolls are kept as cards you can tap to restore and compare, so a good accident never disappears.

## Run it

Open `index.html` in any modern browser. That's the whole thing.

## Deploy

It's a static site, so any static host works.

- **Vercel** — import the repo; no settings needed. The root `index.html` is served automatically.
- **GitHub Pages** — repo Settings → Pages → deploy from `main` / root.
- **Netlify / Cloudflare Pages** — drag the folder in, or connect the repo.

## Tech

Vanilla HTML, CSS, and JavaScript in one file. Fonts (Bricolage Grotesque, Hanken Grotesque, JetBrains Mono) load from Google Fonts. No framework, no bundler.

